  "obligation": "Implement active/passive/declarative element lifecycle and structural indirect calls in the single VM, with complete affected inventories, safe exhaustion and traced cross-instance/program ownership.",
  "representation": "WasmElement stores static mode, type and reference expressions as module facts. Captured bindings own passive WasmElements cells or Undefined dropped state; active segments initialize in declaration order after bounds prechecks and start dropped. ElemDrop and DataDrop share one dropped-binding transition. Function references use ordinary Function cells and the existing weak identity cache. One WasmSignatures pool interns structural types; function indices project into it, and module type indices resolve during lowering. Registered programs share that Rc authority and validate pool-index domains once. Indirect target lookup checks bounds/null/structural type, then direct and indirect calls share argument-window and result-bundle lowering plus the existing dispatcher/activations. Ordinary Wasm calls preserve stack-exhaustion semantics.",
  "worker_stack": "Each shared-suite subprocess reserves a runtime execution thread with quench_stack::WORKER_STACK_SIZE, derived from the same native recursion budget and headroom that the VM guard uses. This is runner reservation, not an alternate executor or altered guest exhaustion threshold.",
